module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Flatness.Flattening.HenselizationFlatteningSituation
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Henselian.Quotient
public import Mathlib.RingTheory.Localization.BaseChange

/-!
# The henselization flatness comparison along a base change of the base ring

`Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_tensorProduct_iff_flat_of_isPushout` compares flatness of `N` over `A`
with flatness of `N' = B' ⊗_B N` over a flat extension `A^h` of `A`, where `C` is a pushout of
`A → A^h` along `A → B` and `B'` is flat over `C` and faithfully flat over `B`. Claim 1 in the
proof of Stacks 05U9 needs the same comparison not over `A` but over a base change `A → R` of the
base: over the quotients `A ⧸ E` and `A^h ⧸ E A^h`, for the powers `E = J^n` of the ideal
generated by the stratification parameters, and over the away localizations `A_a` and
`(A^h)_a`.

Both are the single statement `Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_baseChange_iff_flat_baseChange`: for any
`A`-algebra `R` and any `A^h`-algebra `R^h` making `A → R`, `A → A^h`, `R^h` a pushout square,

`R^h ⊗_{A^h} N'` is flat over `R^h` if and only if `R ⊗_A N` is flat over `R`.

The quotient and away cases are that statement at `R = A ⧸ E`, `R^h = A^h ⧸ E A^h` — a pushout by
`Stacks.Henselian.isPushout_quotient_map` — and at `R = A_a`, `R^h = (A^h)_a` — a pushout by
`Algebra.isPushout_of_isLocalization`. The flatness hypothesis and conclusion are then rewritten
into the `N ⧸ E N` form by `TensorProduct.quotTensorEquivQuotSMul`; in the away case no rewriting
is needed, the tensor product is already the form the source's statement uses.

## Main results

* `Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_baseChange_iff_flat_baseChange`: the comparison along a base change of
  the pushout square. This is the statement the two cases below instantiate.
* `Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_quotient_iff_flat_quotient` and
  `Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_quotient_tensorPrime_iff_flat_quotient`: the quotient case, in general
  and at the distinguished prime of `A^h ⊗_A B`.
* `Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_away_iff_flat_away` and
  `Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_away_tensorPrime_iff_flat_away`: the away case, in general and at the
  distinguished prime.

## Implementation notes

The proof of `flat_baseChange_iff_flat_baseChange` does not base change the whole square: the two
directions use different auxiliary rings, each of which is a tensor product over the ring it has
to be an algebra over, so that every `Algebra` and `IsScalarTower` instance it needs is found by
instance search rather than built by hand.

The forward direction descends along `R ⊗_A B → (R ⊗_A B) ⊗_B B'`, which is faithfully flat
because faithful flatness is stable under base change, after
`TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.distribBaseChange` has written `(R ⊗_A B) ⊗_B N'` as
`((R ⊗_A B) ⊗_B B') ⊗_{R ⊗_A B} ((R ⊗_A B) ⊗_B N)`. The backward direction tensors up along
`R^h → R^h ⊗_{A^h} C`, which is flat because flatness is stable under base change, and uses
`distribBaseChange` over `C` in the other direction. The pushout identifications are
`Algebra.IsPushout.cancelBaseChange` and `TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange`.

The away case is stated for an arbitrary `IsLocalization.Away` of each of the two rings, so that
no algebra structure between them appears in the statement; the one the pushout needs is built in
the proof from `IsLocalization.map`, as Mathlib has no instance for it.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0584](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0584)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05U9](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05U9)
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u v w

open IsLocalRing TensorProduct

namespace Stacks.ResidueFibre

section BaseChange

attribute [local instance] Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra

variable {A : Type*} [CommRing A] {Ah : Type*} [CommRing Ah] [Algebra A Ah] [Module.Flat A Ah]
variable {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
variable {C : Type*} [CommRing C] [Algebra Ah C] [Algebra B C] [Algebra A C]
  [IsScalarTower A Ah C] [IsScalarTower A B C]
variable {B' : Type*} [CommRing B'] [Algebra C B'] [Algebra Ah B'] [Algebra B B'] [Algebra A B']
  [IsScalarTower Ah C B'] [IsScalarTower B C B'] [IsScalarTower A B B'] [IsScalarTower A Ah B']
  [Module.Flat C B'] [Module.FaithfullyFlat B B']
variable {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module B N] [IsScalarTower A B N]
variable (R : Type*) [CommRing R] [Algebra A R]
variable (Rh : Type*) [CommRing Rh] [Algebra A Rh] [Algebra R Rh] [Algebra Ah Rh]
  [IsScalarTower A R Rh] [IsScalarTower A Ah Rh] [Algebra.IsPushout A R Ah Rh]

omit [Algebra C B'] [IsScalarTower Ah C B'] [IsScalarTower B C B'] [Module.Flat C B'] in
/-- The forward half of `Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_baseChange_iff_flat_baseChange`: flatness of
`R^h ⊗_{A^h} N'` over `R^h` descends to flatness of `R ⊗_A N` over `R`.

`R^h` is flat over `R`, being the base change of the flat `A^h`, so `R^h ⊗_{A^h} N'` is flat over
`R`; the pushout identifies it with `R ⊗_A N'` and then with `(R ⊗_A B) ⊗_B N'`, which base
change distributes as `((R ⊗_A B) ⊗_B B') ⊗_{R ⊗_A B} ((R ⊗_A B) ⊗_B N)`. The map
`R ⊗_A B → (R ⊗_A B) ⊗_B B'` is faithfully flat, so Stacks 0584 (2) descends `R`-flatness to
`(R ⊗_A B) ⊗_B N`, which the pushout identifies with `R ⊗_A N`. -/
theorem flat_baseChange_of_flat_baseChange_tensorProduct (hpush : Algebra.IsPushout A Ah B C)
    (h : Module.Flat Rh (Rh ⊗[Ah] (B' ⊗[B] N))) : Module.Flat R (R ⊗[A] N) := by
  have := hpush
  have := h
  have : Module.Flat R Rh :=
    Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv (Algebra.IsPushout.equiv A R Ah Rh).symm.toLinearEquiv
  have : Module.Flat R (Rh ⊗[Ah] (B' ⊗[B] N)) := Module.Flat.trans R Rh _
  have : Module.Flat R (R ⊗[A] (B' ⊗[B] N)) :=
    Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv
      (Algebra.IsPushout.cancelBaseChange A R Ah Rh (B' ⊗[B] N)).symm
  have : Module.Flat R ((R ⊗[A] B) ⊗[B] (B' ⊗[B] N)) :=
    Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv
      (Algebra.IsPushout.cancelBaseChange A R B (R ⊗[A] B) (B' ⊗[B] N))
  have : Module.Flat R (((R ⊗[A] B) ⊗[B] B') ⊗[R ⊗[A] B] ((R ⊗[A] B) ⊗[B] N)) :=
    Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv
      ((TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.distribBaseChange B (R ⊗[A] B) B'
        N).symm.restrictScalars R)
  have : Module.Flat R ((R ⊗[A] B) ⊗[B] N) :=
    (Module.Flat.tensorProduct_iff_of_faithfullyFlat (R := R) (S := R ⊗[A] B)
      (S' := (R ⊗[A] B) ⊗[B] B') (M := (R ⊗[A] B) ⊗[B] N)).mp inferInstance
  exact Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv
    (Algebra.IsPushout.cancelBaseChange A R B (R ⊗[A] B) N).symm

omit [Module.Flat A Ah] [Algebra A B'] [IsScalarTower A B B'] [IsScalarTower A Ah B']
  [Module.FaithfullyFlat B B'] [Algebra.IsPushout A R Ah Rh] in
/-- The backward half of `Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_baseChange_iff_flat_baseChange`: flatness of
`R ⊗_A N` over `R` rises to flatness of `R^h ⊗_{A^h} N'` over `R^h`.

Tensoring up along the flat `R → R^h` and cancelling base changes turns `R`-flatness of `R ⊗_A N`
into `R^h`-flatness of `R^h ⊗_{A^h} (C ⊗_B N)`, hence of `(R^h ⊗_{A^h} C) ⊗_C (C ⊗_B N)`. The
map `R^h ⊗_{A^h} C → (R^h ⊗_{A^h} C) ⊗_C B'` is flat, being a base change of `C → B'`, so
Stacks 0584 (1) gives `R^h`-flatness of
`((R^h ⊗_{A^h} C) ⊗_C B') ⊗_{R^h ⊗_{A^h} C} ((R^h ⊗_{A^h} C) ⊗_C (C ⊗_B N))`, which base change
distributes back as `(R^h ⊗_{A^h} C) ⊗_C (B' ⊗_C (C ⊗_B N))`, i.e. as `R^h ⊗_{A^h} N'`. -/
theorem flat_baseChange_tensorProduct_of_flat_baseChange (hpush : Algebra.IsPushout A Ah B C)
    (h : Module.Flat R (R ⊗[A] N)) : Module.Flat Rh (Rh ⊗[Ah] (B' ⊗[B] N)) := by
  have := hpush
  have := h
  have : Module.Flat Rh (Rh ⊗[A] N) :=
    Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv
      (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange A R Rh Rh N).symm
  have : Module.Flat Rh (Rh ⊗[Ah] (Ah ⊗[A] N)) :=
    Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv
      (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange A Ah Rh Rh N)
  have : Module.Flat Rh (Rh ⊗[Ah] (C ⊗[B] N)) :=
    Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.congr
      (LinearEquiv.refl Rh Rh) (Algebra.IsPushout.cancelBaseChange A Ah B C N))
  have : Module.Flat Rh ((Rh ⊗[Ah] C) ⊗[C] (C ⊗[B] N)) :=
    Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv
      (Algebra.IsPushout.cancelBaseChange Ah Rh C (Rh ⊗[Ah] C) (C ⊗[B] N))
  have : Module.Flat Rh (((Rh ⊗[Ah] C) ⊗[C] B') ⊗[Rh ⊗[Ah] C]
      ((Rh ⊗[Ah] C) ⊗[C] (C ⊗[B] N))) := Module.Flat.tensorProduct_of_flat
  have : Module.Flat Rh ((Rh ⊗[Ah] C) ⊗[C] (B' ⊗[C] (C ⊗[B] N))) :=
    Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv
      ((TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.distribBaseChange C (Rh ⊗[Ah] C) B'
        (C ⊗[B] N)).restrictScalars Rh)
  have : Module.Flat Rh (Rh ⊗[Ah] (B' ⊗[C] (C ⊗[B] N))) :=
    Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv
      (Algebra.IsPushout.cancelBaseChange Ah Rh C (Rh ⊗[Ah] C)
        (B' ⊗[C] (C ⊗[B] N))).symm
  exact Module.Flat.of_linearEquiv (TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.congr
    (LinearEquiv.refl Rh Rh)
    ((TensorProduct.AlgebraTensorModule.cancelBaseChange B C B' B' N).restrictScalars Ah).symm)

/-- **The henselization flatness comparison of Claim 1 of Stacks 05U9 along a base change of the
base ring.** Let `C` be a pushout of `A → A^h` along `A → B`, let `B'` be a `C`-algebra flat over
`C` and faithfully flat over `B`, and write `N' = B' ⊗_B N`. For a base change `A → R` of the base
and a pushout `R^h` of `A → R` along `A → A^h`, the module `R^h ⊗_{A^h} N'` is flat over `R^h`
exactly when `R ⊗_A N` is flat over `R`.

At `R = A` and `R^h = A^h` this is
`Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_tensorProduct_iff_flat_of_isPushout`, up to the identifications of
`A ⊗_A N` with `N` and of `A^h ⊗_{A^h} N'` with `N'`. The cases Claim 1 uses are `R` a quotient of
`A` and `R` an away localization of `A`. -/
theorem flat_baseChange_iff_flat_baseChange (hpush : Algebra.IsPushout A Ah B C) :
    Module.Flat Rh (Rh ⊗[Ah] (B' ⊗[B] N)) ↔ Module.Flat R (R ⊗[A] N) :=
  ⟨flat_baseChange_of_flat_baseChange_tensorProduct R Rh hpush,
    flat_baseChange_tensorProduct_of_flat_baseChange R Rh hpush⟩

end BaseChange

section Cases

attribute [local instance] Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra

variable {A : Type*} [CommRing A] {Ah : Type*} [CommRing Ah] [Algebra A Ah] [Module.Flat A Ah]
variable {B : Type*} [CommRing B] [Algebra A B]
variable {C : Type*} [CommRing C] [Algebra Ah C] [Algebra B C] [Algebra A C]
  [IsScalarTower A Ah C] [IsScalarTower A B C]
variable {B' : Type*} [CommRing B'] [Algebra C B'] [Algebra Ah B'] [Algebra B B'] [Algebra A B']
  [IsScalarTower Ah C B'] [IsScalarTower B C B'] [IsScalarTower A B B'] [IsScalarTower A Ah B']
  [Module.Flat C B'] [Module.FaithfullyFlat B B']
variable {N : Type*} [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module B N] [IsScalarTower A B N]

/-- **The henselization flatness comparison of Claim 1 of Stacks 05U9 over a quotient of the base
ring.** For an ideal `E` of `A`, the module `N' ⧸ (E A^h) N'` is flat over `A^h ⧸ E A^h` exactly
when `N ⧸ E N` is flat over `A ⧸ E`.

This is `Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_baseChange_iff_flat_baseChange` at `R = A ⧸ E` and
`R^h = A^h ⧸ E A^h`, which is a pushout of `A → A ⧸ E` along `A → A^h` by
`Stacks.Henselian.isPushout_quotient_map`, after `TensorProduct.quotTensorEquivQuotSMul` has
rewritten both base changes as quotients. -/
theorem flat_quotient_iff_flat_quotient (hpush : Algebra.IsPushout A Ah B C) (E : Ideal A) :
    Module.Flat (Ah ⧸ E.map (algebraMap A Ah))
        ((B' ⊗[B] N) ⧸
          (E.map (algebraMap A Ah) • ⊤ : Submodule Ah (B' ⊗[B] N))) ↔
      Module.Flat (A ⧸ E) (N ⧸ (E • ⊤ : Submodule A N)) := by
  have : Algebra.IsPushout A (A ⧸ E) Ah (Ah ⧸ E.map (algebraMap A Ah)) :=
    Stacks.Henselian.isPushout_quotient_map E
  rw [Module.Flat.equiv_iff
        ((TensorProduct.quotTensorEquivQuotSMul (B' ⊗[B] N)
          (E.map (algebraMap A Ah))).extendScalarsOfSurjective
            (S := Ah ⧸ E.map (algebraMap A Ah)) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective).symm,
    Module.Flat.equiv_iff
        ((TensorProduct.quotTensorEquivQuotSMul N E).extendScalarsOfSurjective
          (S := A ⧸ E) Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective).symm]
  exact flat_baseChange_iff_flat_baseChange (A ⧸ E) (Ah ⧸ E.map (algebraMap A Ah)) hpush

/-- **The henselization flatness comparison of Claim 1 of Stacks 05U9 over an away localization of
the base ring.** For `a : A`, an away localization `L` of `A` at `a` and an away localization `L^h`
of `A^h` at the image of `a`, the module `L^h ⊗_{A^h} N'` is flat over `L^h` exactly when
`L ⊗_A N` is flat over `L`.

This is `Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_baseChange_iff_flat_baseChange` at `R = L` and `R^h = L^h`: the
square is a pushout because `L^h` is a localization of `A^h` at the image of the multiplicative
set inverted in `L`, which is `Algebra.isPushout_of_isLocalization`. The algebra structure
`L → L^h`, for which Mathlib has no instance, is `IsLocalization.map`. -/
theorem flat_away_iff_flat_away (hpush : Algebra.IsPushout A Ah B C) (a : A)
    (L : Type*) [CommRing L] [Algebra A L] [IsLocalization.Away a L]
    (Lh : Type*) [CommRing Lh] [Algebra Ah Lh] [Algebra A Lh] [IsScalarTower A Ah Lh]
    [IsLocalization.Away (algebraMap A Ah a) Lh] :
    Module.Flat Lh (Lh ⊗[Ah] (B' ⊗[B] N)) ↔ Module.Flat L (L ⊗[A] N) := by
  have hle : Submonoid.powers a ≤
      (Submonoid.powers (algebraMap A Ah a)).comap (algebraMap A Ah) :=
    Submonoid.powers_le.mpr (Submonoid.mem_comap.mpr (Submonoid.mem_powers _))
  let : Algebra L Lh := (IsLocalization.map (M := Submonoid.powers a)
    (T := Submonoid.powers (algebraMap A Ah a)) Lh (algebraMap A Ah) hle).toAlgebra
  have : IsScalarTower A L Lh := IsScalarTower.of_algebraMap_eq' (by
    change algebraMap A Lh = (IsLocalization.map (M := Submonoid.powers a)
      (T := Submonoid.powers (algebraMap A Ah a)) Lh (algebraMap A Ah) hle).comp
        (algebraMap A L)
    rw [IsLocalization.map_comp, ← IsScalarTower.algebraMap_eq A Ah Lh])
  have : Algebra.IsPushout A L Ah Lh :=
    Algebra.IsPushout.symm (Algebra.isPushout_of_isLocalization (Submonoid.powers a) L Ah Lh)
  exact flat_baseChange_iff_flat_baseChange L Lh hpush

end Cases

section Henselization

attribute [local instance] Algebra.TensorProduct.rightAlgebra

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
variable {B : Type v} [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing B] [Algebra A B]
  [IsLocalHom (algebraMap A B)]
variable {N : Type w} [AddCommGroup N] [Module A N] [Module B N] [IsScalarTower A B N]
variable (Ah : Type u) [CommRing Ah] [IsLocalRing Ah] [Algebra A Ah]
  [IsLocalRing.IsHenselization A (ResidueField A) Ah]

/-- **Flatness over a local ring and over its henselization, over a quotient of the base.** Let
`A → B` be a local homomorphism of local rings, let `A^h` be a henselization of `A` and let `B'`
be the localization of `A^h ⊗_A B` at the maximal ideal `𝔪_B ⊗ A^h + B ⊗ 𝔪_{A^h}`. For an ideal
`E` of `A` and `N' = B' ⊗_B N`, the module `N' ⧸ (E A^h) N'` is flat over `A^h ⧸ E A^h` exactly
when `N ⧸ E N` is flat over `A ⧸ E`.

At `E = ⊥` this specialises to `Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_localization_tensorPrime_iff_flat`, up
to the identification of `A ⧸ ⊥` with `A`. This is the comparison that Claim 1 of the proof of
Stacks 05U9 needs for the powers `E = J^n` of the ideal generated by its stratification
parameters. -/
theorem flat_quotient_tensorPrime_iff_flat_quotient (E : Ideal A) :
    Module.Flat (Ah ⧸ E.map (algebraMap A Ah))
        ((Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah) ⊗[B] N) ⧸
          (E.map (algebraMap A Ah) • ⊤ :
            Submodule Ah (Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah) ⊗[B] N))) ↔
      Module.Flat (A ⧸ E) (N ⧸ (E • ⊤ : Submodule A N)) := by
  have : Module.Flat A Ah := IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.flat (L := ResidueField A)
  have : Module.FaithfullyFlat B (Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah)) :=
    faithfullyFlat_localizationTensorPrime Ah
  exact flat_quotient_iff_flat_quotient (C := Ah ⊗[A] B) inferInstance E

/-- **Flatness over a local ring and over its henselization, over an away localization of the
base.** In the situation of
`Stacks.ResidueFibre.flat_quotient_tensorPrime_iff_flat_quotient`, for `a : A` the module
`(A^h)_a ⊗_{A^h} N'` is flat over `(A^h)_a` exactly when `A_a ⊗_A N` is flat over `A_a`.

This is the comparison that Claim 1 of the proof of Stacks 05U9 needs to transport the flatness of
the strata of its generic flatness stratification to the henselization. -/
theorem flat_away_tensorPrime_iff_flat_away (a : A) :
    Module.Flat (Localization.Away (algebraMap A Ah a))
        (Localization.Away (algebraMap A Ah a) ⊗[Ah]
          (Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah) ⊗[B] N)) ↔
      Module.Flat (Localization.Away a) (Localization.Away a ⊗[A] N) := by
  have : Module.Flat A Ah := IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.flat (L := ResidueField A)
  have : Module.FaithfullyFlat B (Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah)) :=
    faithfullyFlat_localizationTensorPrime Ah
  exact flat_away_iff_flat_away (C := Ah ⊗[A] B) inferInstance a (Localization.Away a)
    (Localization.Away (algebraMap A Ah a))

variable {ι : Type*} (g : ι → A)

/-- **The hypothesis `hU` of the inner step of Claim 1 of Stacks 05U9, over the henselization.**
Given the flatness of `N` on the away localizations of `A` at a family `g`, the base change
`N' = B' ⊗_B N` is flat on the away localizations of `A^h` at the image family.

This is the hypothesis `hU` of `Stacks.flat_of_least_flattening_of_flat_away` for the base `A^h`,
the module `N'` and the family `fun i ↦ algebraMap A A^h (g i)`. -/
theorem forall_flat_away_tensorPrime_of_forall_flat_away
    (hU : ∀ i, Module.Flat (Localization.Away (g i)) (Localization.Away (g i) ⊗[A] N)) :
    ∀ i, Module.Flat (Localization.Away (algebraMap A Ah (g i)))
      (Localization.Away (algebraMap A Ah (g i)) ⊗[Ah]
        (Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah) ⊗[B] N)) :=
  fun i ↦ (flat_away_tensorPrime_iff_flat_away Ah (g i)).mpr (hU i)

/-- **The hypothesis `hpow` of the inner step of Claim 1 of Stacks 05U9, over the
henselization.** Given the flatness of `N ⧸ J^n N` over `A ⧸ J^n` for the ideal `J` generated by a
family `g` and every `n > 0`, the base change `N' = B' ⊗_B N` has the same property over `A^h` for
the ideal generated by the image family, which is `J A^h`.

This is the hypothesis `hpow` of `Stacks.flat_of_least_flattening_of_flat_away` for the base
`A^h`, the module `N'` and the family `fun i ↦ algebraMap A A^h (g i)`. -/
theorem forall_flat_quotient_pow_tensorPrime_of_forall_flat_quotient_pow
    (hpow : ∀ n : ℕ, 0 < n → Module.Flat (A ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range g) ^ n)
      (N ⧸ ((Ideal.span (Set.range g) ^ n) • (⊤ : Submodule A N)))) :
    ∀ n : ℕ, 0 < n →
      Module.Flat (Ah ⧸ Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ algebraMap A Ah (g i)) ^ n)
        ((Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah) ⊗[B] N) ⧸
          ((Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ algebraMap A Ah (g i)) ^ n) •
            (⊤ : Submodule Ah
              (Localization.AtPrime (tensorPrime (A := A) (B := B) Ah) ⊗[B] N)))) := by
  intro n hn
  have hspan : Ideal.span (Set.range fun i ↦ algebraMap A Ah (g i)) ^ n =
      (Ideal.span (Set.range g) ^ n).map (algebraMap A Ah) := by
    rw [Ideal.map_pow, Ideal.map_span, ← Set.range_comp]
    rfl
  rw [hspan]
  exact (flat_quotient_tensorPrime_iff_flat_quotient Ah (Ideal.span (Set.range g) ^ n)).mpr
    (hpow n hn)

end Henselization

end Stacks.ResidueFibre

end
